main='''<main id="main"><div class="atlas-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Overview</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/evidence/">Evidence</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Boundary benchmark</span></div><div class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">21 October 2026 · Boundary benchmark 0.1</div><h1>Boundary treatment helps.<br>It cannot restore excluded content.</h1><p class="lede">Six known synthetic signals compare periodic projection, zero padding, reflection padding and Hann taper/division. The empirical reconstruction gate stays unchanged.</p></div><aside class="callout"><strong>Synthetic comparison · Development — no registry entry · Physical promotion 0</strong><p>No method passes all six cases. Independent review is pending. The previous 0/891 empirical gate result and EXIT-03 HOLD remain intact. No experimental rerun or action estimate is reported.</p></aside><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/sources/boundary-benchmark-v0.1/REPORT.md">Read report and bounds ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/boundary-benchmark-v0.1/CONTRACT.json">Inspect frozen setup</a></div><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">01</div><div><h2>Smooth-signal recovery differs from full-state recovery.</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Synthetic passes</th><th>Limit exposed</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Periodic</td><td>2 / 6</td><td>Boundary mismatch affects smooth transients</td></tr><tr><td>Zero pad</td><td>4 / 6</td><td>Pulse and omitted-sideband failures</td></tr><tr><td>Reflect pad</td><td>4 / 6</td><td>Pulse and omitted-sideband failures</td></tr><tr><td>Hann / divide</td><td>4 / 6</td><td>Improves smooth cases, increases pulse error</td></tr></tbody></table><p>These ground-truth-based synthetic gates differ from the empirical residual gate; their pass rates are not interchangeable. Complex RMS and phase both enter. All 24 evaluations are retained.</p><p>The omitted sideband has amplitude 0.3. Every method’s full-state relative RMS error is about 0.287, even when its fundamental-only error is small. Recovering a selected carrier is a distinct objective from recovering the full signal.</p><a class="text-link" href="/sources/boundary-benchmark-v0.1/METRICS.csv">All synthetic metrics ↓</a></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">02</div><div><h2>A guard leaves boundary influence.</h2><p>The explicit DFT projection kernel gives a conditional error bound from outside-sample uncertainty. A unit impulse just outside the measured segment has a nonzero interior effect even after discarding 1024 samples at each end.</p><p>For the fixed padded filter, the outside-row absolute sum ranges approximately 1.06749–1.64220 across the interior. Multiplying it by an independently justified uniform continuation-error bound yields a numerical reconstruction budget. No such physical bound is established here.</p><p>Padding agreement does not certify the unknown continuation. The Hann method changes the operator and needs its own division-error analysis. Constructor floating-point checks are not formal interval arithmetic.</p><a class="text-link" href="/sources/boundary-benchmark-v0.1/RESULTS.json">Kernel and reconstruction results →</a></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">03</div><div><h2>Next: an estimator using only measured samples.</h2><p>Freeze a finite-support quadrature kernel, its delay, transfer response and valid interior before another experimental run. This can remove assumed padded samples from the estimate; it does not certify unrestricted dynamics outside the record.</p><p>The present synthetic controls distinguish boundary mismatch from excluded content in known cases. They do not apportion the causes of the experimental phase-gate failure. Acquisition gain/skew, full energy, absolute native support and the action anchor remain open.</p><a class="text-link" href="/sources/boundary-benchmark-v0.1/benchmark.py">Reproduction code ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/evidence/signed-reconstruction/">Preserved reconstruction v0.1 →</a></div></section></main>'''
